{title: 598 - Watch, Ye Saints}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #598 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 598}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/F]Watch, ye [G]saints, with eyelids [C]waking;
[C]Lo! the powers of heaven are shaking;
[C]Keep your lamps all [G]trimmed and burning,
[G]Ready for your Lord’s [G7]returning.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]Lo! He comes, lo! Jesus comes;
[C]Lo! He come, He comes all glorious!
[C/E]Jesus comes [G]to reign [C]victorious,
[C]Lo! He comes, [Am]yes, Jesus comes.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/F]Lo! the [G]promise of your [C]Savior,
[C]Pardoned sin and purchased favor,
[C]Blood-washed robes and [G]crowns of glory;
[G]Haste to tell redemption's [G7]story.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/F]Kingdoms [G]at their base are [C]crumbling,
[C]Hark! His chariot wheels are rumbling;
[C]Tell, O tell of [G]grace abounding,
[G]While the seventh trump [G7]is sounding.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/F]Nations wane, [G]though proud and stately;
[C]Christ His kingdom hasteneth greatly;
[C]Earth her latest [G]pangs is summing;
[G]Shout, ye saints, your Lord [G7]is coming.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm/F]Sinners, come, [G]while Christ is [C]pleading;
[C]Now for you He's interceding;
[C]Haste, ere grace and [G]time diminished
[G]Shall proclaim the mystery [G7]finished.
{end_of_verse}
